,P(0)=2.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. For which value of $P$ is the number of turtles that developed fungus growing at the fastest possible rate?" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324678 1113 #uuid "3451059c-1c4e-54f9-9dc9-14e12f6043d8" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324678 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.6P-0.012{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.012P(50-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=50.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $50,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 50=25.\n$$" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324680 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324681 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324682 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324683 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324684 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1041 "selection" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324683 13194139534983 true] [17592186324679 1110 #uuid "6a33dc90-988c-53e7-a11e-45433f2ccbe3" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324680 1034 "12" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534983 true] [17592186324680 1111 #uuid "8797f27b-8233-5dbf-912c-84d80a18578a" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324681 1034 "50" 13194139534983 true] [17592186324681 1103 #ed